\label{CylEner_prp}
If $(X,J)$ is an almost complex manifold and $g$ is a Riemannian metric on~$X$, then 
there exist continuous functions $\delta_{J,g},\hbar_{J,g},C_{J,g}\!:X\!\longrightarrow\!\mathbb R^+$
with the following properties.
If \hbox{$u\!:[-R,R]\!\times\!S^1\!\longrightarrow\!X$} is a \hbox{$J$-holomorphic} map such that
$\textnormal{Im}\,u\subset B_{\delta_{J,g}(u(0,1))}^g(u(0,1))$, then 
\BE{CylEner_e}
E_g\big(u;[-R\!+\!T,R\!-\!T]\!\times\!S^1\big) \le 
C_{J,g}\big(u(1,0)\big)\textnormal{e}^{-T}E_g(u) \qquad\forall~T\ge0\,.\end{equation}
If in addition $E_g(u)<\hbar_{J,g}\big(u(0,1)\big)$, then
\BE{CylEner_e2}
\textnormal{diam}_g\big(u([-R\!+\!T,R\!-\!T]\!\times\!S^1)\big)
\le C_{J,g}\big(u(1,0)\big) \textnormal{e}^{-T/2}\sqrt{E_g(u)} \quad\forall~T\ge1\,.\end{equation}

